{"author":"Rebar Bot Nava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nCites re-measured on origin/main 403719c01ce (base 083620b0 drifted).\n`_ALIASES={}` (`_config_sections.py:200`) is empty since ADR 0116 yet still threaded through 4 modules. The env-alias half — `_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES`/`_map_legacy_env` — **already landed** under sibling 25a4 (`e096a33d3b7`); neither exists in `src`, and `_config_sources.py` (317 lines) keeps only prose. 13 warn tombstones (7 env `_deprecations.py:140-148` + 6 cfg `:157,158,162,164,168,169`) are inert and all claim `removed_in=\"v1.0.0\"`; `_tomb` (`:127-129`) hardcodes `_MAJOR` (`:27`). `[llm]` is reserved (`_config_sections.py:211`, `continue` `:226`), so `[llm] overlap_k = 5` is accepted silently even under `REBAR_CONFIG_UNKNOWN_KEYS=error`; the overlap epic needs removed `overlap_*` keys to warn. The alias loop (`:245-250`, -3 McCabe) and the `[llm]` branch must land together: `coerce_sparse` (`:214`) is **exactly 15** against `max-complexity = 15`, so the branch alone breaks C901. Removed env names never warn: `env_overrides()` (`:296`) reads only live `_SECTIONS` keys, so a set `REBAR_PUSH` is ignored; only cfg keys reach `_warn_unknown`.\n\n## Approach\n**Aliases.** Delete `config.py:9` (sole alias import; `:45,56` unrelated, `:382-385` is tombstone machinery this story KEEPS); `_config_schema.py:32`; `_config_sections.py:198-200,246-250` (rewrite `:245` to `warn_deprecated_cfg_keys(sect, d, logger=logger)`; drop the unused `warn_deprecated` import `:22`); `show_config.py:142-146`. `gen_env_registry.py:405`: attribution becomes `\"src/rebar/_deprecations.py (deprecation registry)\"` — no output change, since `_env_aliases()` (`:384`) returns `{}` (sole `REGISTRY` row is `cfg`-kind) so the `:404` loop never runs. Docstring `:19` already cites `REGISTRY`. Keep `REGISTRY`/`warn_deprecated`/`warn_deprecated_cfg_keys` (future channel).\n\n**Tombstones.** `_tomb(..., *, removed_in: str)` — keyword-required, no `_MAJOR` default (`_MAJOR` stays for `_scheduled`, `:42`). `_TOMBSTONE_REGISTRY` (`:135`) becomes exactly six error rows: `TICKETS_TRACKER_DIR` (`:137`), `REBAR_MCP_ALLOW_RECONCILE_LIVE` (`:138`), cfg `verify.require_verdict_for_close` (`:150-155`), file `.rebar/config.conf` (`:171`), `REBAR_LLM_MAX_ITERS` (`:173`) at `v0.8.0`; `REBAR_LLM_MODEL` (`:176`) at `v0.12.0`. `warn` stays vocabulary (`_TOMBSTONE_BEHAVIORS` `:74`, pinned by `test_tombstone_registry.py:71`); templates unchanged (`show_config.py:180,182`, `_deprecations.py:186-193,280`).\n\n**`[llm]` warn.** Add `_LLM_KNOWN_KEYS: tuple[str, ...]` next to `_RESERVED_SECTIONS` (`:211`): the 15 keys read in `config_readers.py` + the three `llm/` modules, plus `evals`. Replace `:225-226`: for `sect == \"llm\"` with a dict value, `_warn_unknown(\"llm\", <keys not in _LLM_KNOWN_KEYS>, source, strict=strict)`, then `continue`. No `rebar.llm` import (docstring `:206` rule). Messages reuse the `_config_coercion.py:88` templates keyed `llm.<key>`.\n\n**Sync test** `tests/unit/test_config_llm_known_keys.py::test_llm_known_keys_match_config_readers`: AST-walk `config_readers.py` for each `_llm_str/_llm_int/_llm_float/_llm_str_source` call (4th positional literal) and the three `llm/` modules for `table.get(\"<lit>\")`; assert `set(_LLM_KNOWN_KEYS) - {\"evals\"} == collected` and `\"evals\" in _LLM_KNOWN_KEYS` (the eval epic deletes that carve-out with its reader). Equality is exact, so this depends on the overlap epic's removal story (`granitic-realisable-dolphin`, `09a8-5436-6b65-479c`).\n\n**Docs.** `docs/api-stability.md:27` (alias -> registry sentence; keep `:30-34`); `docs/config.md` `## Back-compat` `:841` / tombstones `:855-902` (default `warn` unchanged per `_config_sources.py:312-317`, `[llm]` warns; no alias tables; `:886-902` -> six error rows + a no-warn-tombstones sentence); `scripts/gen_config_reference.py:224-233` (`_cfg_tombstones`) + `:342-346` (`Removed in` column), regenerate `docs/config-reference.md`; `test_gen_config_reference.py:255-267` asserts `tomb.removed_in in row`; `tests/golden/config_surface.json` unchanged.\n\n**Tests.** Delete alias/tombstone assertions in the Scope test files (incl. `test_config_surface_golden.py:52,54` and the `:177` docstring). Add `test_tombstone_registry.py::test_every_tombstone_names_its_real_removal_release` (each row `^v0\\.\\d+\\.\\d+$`, none `v1.0.0`) and `::test_only_error_class_rows_remain`; `test_config_backcompat.py::test_unknown_llm_key_warns_like_a_core_key` (caplog `unknown key 'llm.bogus'`), `::test_unknown_llm_key_errors_under_strict`, `::test_known_llm_key_never_warns`.\n\n**Release note** (`docs/release-notes.md` + `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]`), one BREAKING (pre-1.0) entry: 13 warn tombstones retired — 7 env names unread (silent), 6 cfg keys become ordinary unknown keys, six error rows name their release, unknown `[tool.rebar.llm]` keys warn.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/`: `_config_sections.py`, `_config_schema.py`, `config.py`, `_commands/show_config.py`, `_deprecations.py`. `scripts/`: `gen_env_registry.py`, `gen_config_reference.py`. Docs: `config.md`, `config-reference.md`, `api-stability.md`, `release-notes.md`, `CHANGELOG.md`. `tests/unit/`: `test_config_alias_overlap_rename.py`, `test_config_show.py`, `test_config_surface_golden.py`, `test_config_backcompat.py`, `test_config_resolved_statuses_removal.py`, `test_gen_config_reference.py`, new `test_config_llm_known_keys.py`; `tests/interfaces/contracts/test_tombstone_registry.py`. `REBAR_CONFIG_UNKNOWN_KEYS` default stays `warn`. Out of scope: `_config_sources.py` (25a4 removed its alias code; only prose remains); `llm/config.py`, `_config_schema.py:81-84`, `overlap_*` in `config_readers.py` (overlap epic); `REBAR_RECONCILER_FAIL_SILENT_NOOP` (reconciler epic); `[llm.evals]` reader (eval epic). `tests/fixtures/**` is frozen corpus quoting these names; never edited.\n\n## Testing\n- `[llm] overlap_k = 5`: `rebar config validate` -> exit 0 (skips reserved, `show_config.py:129`); `rebar list` logs `unknown key 'llm.overlap_k' ignored`; `REBAR_CONFIG_UNKNOWN_KEYS=error rebar list` -> non-zero naming `llm.overlap_k`.\n- `TICKETS_TRACKER_DIR=x rebar list` -> non-zero naming `v0.8.0` + `REBAR_TRACKER_DIR`; `... config validate` prints `ERROR: env TICKETS_TRACKER_DIR was removed in v0.8.0...`; `REBAR_LLM_MODEL=x rebar review-plan <id> --status` -> error naming `v0.12.0`.\n- `[code_health] enabled = true`: `rebar list` -> exit 0, logs `unknown key 'code_health.enabled' ignored`; `REBAR_PUSH=off rebar list` -> exit 0, silent.\n- The three generator `--check`s (`gen_config_reference`, `generate_config_surface_golden`, `gen_env_registry`); `ruff check --select C901 src/rebar/_config_sections.py` (coerce_sparse 13, was 15); `make verify`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] AC1 `git grep -nE '(^|[^A-Za-z0-9_])(_ALIASES|_LEGACY_ENV_ALIASES|_map_legacy_env)([^A-Za-z0-9_]|$)' -- src tests scripts ':(exclude)tests/fixtures'` returns **no hits** (it returns exactly 9 today — confirm that before implementing, or the AC proves nothing). Do NOT write `\\b` under `-E`: git grep's ERE engine ignores it and the command matches nothing, passing vacuously. Both the identifier binding and the exclude are required — a bare `_ALIASES\\b` also matches `_HIDDEN_ALIASES`, `_ARCH_ALIASES`, `_EDIT_FLAG_ALIASES`, `_REMOVED_SIMPLE_CLI_ALIASES`, `_DEPRECATED_PROVIDER_ALIASES` (21 live out-of-scope hits) plus 3 corpus JSONs.\n- [x] AC2 `tombstones()` returns exactly 6 rows, all `behavior==\"error\"`, `removed_in` = `v0.8.0` x5 + `v0.12.0` x1 (two new `test_tombstone_registry.py` tests). Baseline: 19 = 6 error + 13 warn.\n- [x] AC3 The three CLI commands above produce the quoted text (interfaces tests; `test_error_env_var_fails_loud:124` asserts `removed_in in out`). `config.py:382-385` must stay intact — AC3 depends on it.\n- [x] AC4 Unknown `[llm]` keys warn/error per policy, known keys never warn (three new `test_config_backcompat.py` tests); sync test green.\n- [x] AC5 All three generator `--check`s clean; `coerce_sparse` at 13 via `ruff --select C901`; `make verify` green."}},"env_id":"492a5c71-6cda-48a6-8134-02ff6a672739","event_type":"EDIT","timestamp":1793439132695285001,"uuid":"49c6305a-7d9e-4dd1-b7bd-088635cadb6a"}